  "releaseNotes": "- Uses one Schema editor for published API input and result fields, including\n  nested objects, array children, local references, sibling additions and deletion;\n  input fields omit the result-source column\n- Exposes independent required-property and nullable-value controls for input and\n  result fields, preserving the imported Schema constraints and creation defaults\n- Enforces the complete saved input Schema at invocation with the existing shared\n  validator; previously ignored enum, array-item, additional-property and nullable\n  rules now apply, with input failures reported before agent execution\n- Keeps input identities, result-source bindings and message-template variables\n  synchronized during field and parent renames, and rejects deletion of inputs\n  still referenced by the configuration\n- Generates request example structure through the existing Schema library rather\n  than a flat field projection; actual values must satisfy the configured constraints\n- Aligns field headers and controls with shared column widths and adapts to the\n  editor's available width, including expanded navigation and narrow screens\n- Reuses Runtime `1.0.0-beta.31`; existing sandbox templates remain unchanged",
